From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:49:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] census: track a Coherent surface's rows as ranges, not
 the whole surface

A surface's pages past its texture rows (an IOSurface's trailing pages, a
second plane) were armed and held with the rows, so a CPU or DMA touch
there met no pending page, came back as a bare -EFAULT and fused the
census (B1). census_coh_track(start, len) now tracks [start, start+len)
as one of up to four ranges of the surface; pages outside every range
stay OPEN, untrack frees one range, and touches outside the ranges pass
straight through.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
